VeridianOS: predicate parser: keep the elements of a string list in order

Real bug, found with 0002's fix (and prepared for upstream,
invent.kde.org/frameworks/solid). string_list_rec is right-recursive
(VAL_STRING ',' string_list_rec), so the parser builds the list from its
last element and PredicateParse_appendStringListValue() is called with
each earlier element in turn; appending reversed the list:
"{'a', 'b', 'c'}" became c, b, a, and could never match a property
value. The element is now prepended.

--- a/src/solid/devices/predicateparse.cpp
+++ b/src/solid/devices/predicateparse.cpp
@@ -210,7 +210,8 @@
 
     QStringList new_list = variant->toStringList();
 
-    new_list << QString::fromLatin1(name);
+    // string_list_rec is right-recursive: name comes before the elements already in the list
+    new_list.prepend(QString::fromLatin1(name));
 
     delete variant;
     free(name);
